Why did I feel like crying? My chest hurt, my stomach felt twisted in anxious knots, yet I had no context for any of it. My hands sat primly in my lap, or so my senses told me as I could no more turn my gaze downwards to peer at them than I could bring one up for scrutiny.

I was here, wherever here was. I was... someone, yet this someone wasn't me. Or, at least not only me, or even predominantly me.

*This was a dumb idea.*

