My thoughts-- or that insidious foreign pull that felt so close to them-- focused on the empty patch of dirt I'd been observing. It imagined a person there. The details were nebulous: a woman or older teen, warm and cheerfu--

Comforting. Not cheerful, but comforting. That distinction mattered, of that I was certain.

A comforting older teen. I pictured her looking at her hands, and she did. The foreign thoughts didn't oppose it. I had the imaginary figure look around, and she followed through, though my own field of vision didn't change.

A faint, distant hint of hope bloomed in me. Shameful hope, but a seed all the same.

I tilted the woman's head. Was I meant to be the puppeteer of someone's imaginary friend? It's not like I could see anything new with the avatar, nor interact with anything either. I didn't even know the name-- *Gwion*-- of my body...

Gwion?

