It took some time for the next flash of feeling and intent to be communicated to me: annoyance at the noise. There had been more I might have been interested in, but my priority didn't lay in my own curiosity, so I suggested we take a stroll through a nearby garden.

The quiet helped. The ball of feelings had receeded, and I felt more whole than I'd started as. Gwion's hand trailed along patches of flowers.

I felt myself fade.

