There shouldn't have been that much understanding in the face of a seven years old. The girl nodded quickly and didn't linger when I told her to scoot.

I was left alone with myself in the kid's room, apparently steeling myself for a face-off with an abusive parent.

"Gwion, how can I help?" I offered. I'd gotten the gist of the situation, and felt any missing blank would be filled in in short order.

He didn't answer, neither in thoughts nor emotional bleedthrough. But our gaze focused on my avatar. An amorphous presence that had no eyes for him to meet, and yet I had the unmistakable feeling of being seen.






